  === parent-live: container output readers check on disposable container ===
  container_image=agentbox-desktop:0.1 network_mode=none
  exec_run(demux=True) 2MiB stream buffered in docker-py: 2097152 bytes (uncapped in-memory buffer before _truncate)
  exec_start(stream=True, demux=True) with _Head(): kept=65537 bytes, total=2097152 bytes, truncated=True
Parent-live confirms that exec_run buffers full 2 MiB stream in docker-py, while exec_start with _Head caps retained bytes to 65537.

=== Conclusion ===
Verification confirmed the source-level inconsistency in container output readers:
1. exec uses streaming _Head (64 KiB cap) and _timed(t, kill_after=5).
2. read_file and outbox_read use head -c and _timed(_READ_TIMEOUT).
3. workspace_manifest uses head -c and _timed(_MANIFEST_TIMEOUT).
4. preview _walk uses head -z -n $limit and _timed(_PREVIEW_TIMEOUT).
5. list_dir and outbox_list lack both container-side timeouts and output byte caps.
6. preview _expand has _PREVIEW_TIMEOUT (10s) but lacks record and byte caps before buffering full glob matches.
7. screenshot cats full PNG image without streaming byte cap.
However, demonstrating fatal control-plane memory exhaustion (OOM kill) or threadpool hang under large-scale container output requires running against a live Docker daemon with real containers, which is excluded from the subagent sandbox environment.
Verdict remains needs_validation.
